      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the bounds check needs fixing, since `vma_pages()` counts 4KB pages. aosp/4368058 already uses a pattern for this in kernel/dma: `vm_pgoff + vma_kernel_pages(vma)` against the size in kernel pages, where `vma_kernel_pages()` includes `vm_slice_off`.\n\nWould using `vma_kernel_pages()` in the existing checks, here and in `dma_buf_mmap()`, be enough? \n\nThat would avoid `vma_aligned_size()` here.\n\nOne more thing I noticed: rounding dmabuf-\u003esize up to the VMA page size also changes native behaviour, since a native process could now map the partial last page of an unaligned dma-buf, which the old size \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT check refused.",
      "isAi": true,
