      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:43:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you help me understand why `vm_slice_off` is reset here?\n\n`@pgoff` is in kernel pages and can\u0027t carry the 4KB offset the process passed to the importer\u0027s `mmap()`, so I think this maps the buffer up to 12KB before the requested offset.\n\nWould it work to keep `vma_slice_off(vma)`, which `vma_kernel_pages()` then bounds, or to return `-EINVAL` for a non-zero slice as `perf_mmap()` does?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "3026c0aef0d9171b2f15600e2bd9c12d8fb8de04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
