      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:43:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this branch and `remap_pfn_range_slice()` might not be needed anymore: since aosp/4368055, `remap_pfn_range()` in a 4KB VMA maps 4KB frames starting at the slice that `vma_slice_offset()` gives the address.\n\nAs far as I can tell, the native loop only breaks because it remaps a whole kernel page from `vm_start`, which runs into `pfn + 1` when `vm_slice_off !\u003d 0` and past `vm_end` when the last page is partial.\n\nWould clamping the size in the existing loop work for you? Something like:\n\n```\n    unsigned long off \u003d (unsigned long)vma_slice_off(vma) \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT_4KB;\n    ...\n        unsigned long size \u003d min(PAGE_SIZE - off, vma-\u003evm_end - addr);\n\n        ret \u003d remap_pfn_range(vma, addr, page_to_pfn(page), size,\n                              vma-\u003evm_page_prot);\n        ...\n        addr +\u003d size;\n        off \u003d 0;\n\n```\n\nNative VMAs have `off \u003d\u003d 0` and whole pages, so they wouldn\u0027t change.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "3026c0aef0d9171b2f15600e2bd9c12d8fb8de04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
